{
  "task": {
    "id": "Prob078_dualedge",
    "spec": "\r\nI would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following\r\ninterface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise\r\nspecified.\r\n\r\n - input  clk\r\n - input  d\r\n - output q\r\n\r\nA dual-edge triggered flip-flop is triggered on both edges of the clock.\r\nHowever, FPGAs don't have dual-edge triggered flip-flops, and using an\r\nalways @(posedge clk or negedge clk) is not accepted as a legal\r\nsensitivity list. Build a circuit that functionally behaves like a\r\ndual-edge triggered flip-flop.\r\n\r\n",
    "interface": {
      "top": "TopModule",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "clk",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "d",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "q",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "constraints": "SystemVerilog, exactly one self-contained TopModule DUT. Inline all helper logic inside TopModule; do not define auxiliary modules. xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."
  },
  "sample_id": "272d7c6c-f647-4c18-ad2e-328233e4ffac",
  "variant_id": "C",
  "current": {
    "revision_id": "6faed42c-8e6b-47b1-8793-79908a7b244a",
    "source_sha256": "e1b4de135865ed2b6e2219b1c91f774c81ef3d2c2bca49d05a4f3050530db083",
    "source": "\nmodule TopModule(\n    input  clk,\n    input  d,\n    output q\n);\n\n    reg q_pos;\n    reg q_neg;\n\n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        q_pos <= d;\n    end\n\n    always @(negedge clk) begin\n        q_neg <= d;\n    end\n\n    assign q = clk ? q_pos : q_neg;\n\nendmodule\n"
  },
